# Aurora __VERSION__ — Installation

Self-contained offline package. **No source code** is included — only container
images, Helm chart, compose files, and install guides.

## What's in the box

```
images/
  aurora-api-__VERSION__.tar
  aurora-web-__VERSION__.tar
  aurora-workers-__VERSION__.tar
charts/aurora-__VERSION__.tgz
docker-compose.trial.yml
.env.trial.example
k8s/                    # optional raw manifests (k3s / plain kubectl)
LICENSE
INSTALL.md              # this file
AFTER-TRIAL.md
```

## Licensing

- **Days 1–30:** full product, no key required (clock starts on first DB contact).
- **After day 30:** API returns HTTP 402 until you set `AURORA_LICENSE_KEY`.
- **Keys:** email **sales@zyvor.dev**.

Check status anytime:

```bash
curl -s https://<your-host>/api/v1/license/status | jq
```

## Prerequisites

- Docker **or** Podman (for compose / image load)
- **or** Kubernetes / k3s + Helm 3 (recommended production path)
- Backing services: Postgres, Redis, Qdrant, Neo4j, MinIO, and an LLM
  (Ollama local or OpenAI via `LLM_PROVIDER` / `OPENAI_API_KEY`)

## Path A — Docker / Podman Compose (fastest eval)

```bash
# Load images (Podman: replace docker with podman)
docker load -i images/aurora-api-__VERSION__.tar
docker load -i images/aurora-web-__VERSION__.tar
docker load -i images/aurora-workers-__VERSION__.tar

cp .env.trial.example .env
# edit .env — especially SECRET_KEY and NEXT_PUBLIC / FRONTEND URLs

docker compose -f docker-compose.trial.yml --env-file .env up -d
# Podman: podman compose -f docker-compose.trial.yml --env-file .env up -d
```

Open the URL you set for the web UI. Default admin seed (change immediately):
`marketing@zyvor.dev` / `Admin@321` (disable with `SEED_DEFAULT_ADMIN=false`).

## Path B — Helm (k3s / Kubernetes)

```bash
# Load images onto every node (or push to your registry and retag values)
docker load -i images/aurora-api-__VERSION__.tar
docker load -i images/aurora-web-__VERSION__.tar
docker load -i images/aurora-workers-__VERSION__.tar
# k3s:
sudo k3s ctr images import images/aurora-api-__VERSION__.tar
sudo k3s ctr images import images/aurora-web-__VERSION__.tar
sudo k3s ctr images import images/aurora-workers-__VERSION__.tar

helm install aurora charts/aurora-__VERSION__.tgz \
  --namespace aurora --create-namespace \
  --set env.DATABASE_URL='postgresql+asyncpg://…' \
  --set env.REDIS_URL='redis://…' \
  --set env.QDRANT_URL='http://…' \
  --set env.NEO4J_URI='bolt://…' \
  --set env.NEO4J_PASSWORD='…' \
  --set env.MINIO_ENDPOINT='…' \
  --set env.MINIO_ACCESS_KEY='…' \
  --set env.MINIO_SECRET_KEY='…' \
  --set env.OLLAMA_BASE_URL='http://…/v1' \
  --set env.SECRET_KEY="$(openssl rand -hex 32)" \
  --set env.FRONTEND_URL='https://aurora.example.com'
```

Optional ingress: `--set ingress.enabled=true --set ingress.host=aurora.example.com`.

After trial:

```bash
helm upgrade aurora charts/aurora-__VERSION__.tgz --reuse-values \
  --set license.key='<key-from-sales@zyvor.dev>'
kubectl -n aurora rollout restart deploy
```

## Path C — Raw k3s / kubectl manifests

See `k8s/` and apply with `kubectl apply -f k8s/` after loading images and
creating an `aurora-env` Secret from your `.env`.

